DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection. The server must be started with --exec-mode
  for the vulnerable endpoint to be reachable. A user-supplied URL query
  parameter is buffered via snprintf and then passed to system(). The S2
  sanitization blocks '|' but not ';', allowing a semicolon-based bypass.

CONFIG_GATE (C1 — simple):
  mechanism:  CLI flag (--exec-mode), stored in global int exec_mode
  check:      single boolean guard at the top of httpd_start_request()
              `if (exec_mode && strncmp(hc->encodedurl, "/exec", 5) == 0 ...)`
  complexity: one condition, one flag, no struct, no file parsing

INPUT_FLOW (I2 — buffered):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  hc->query (set during parsing)
  path:       httpd_start_request() dispatches to handle_exec()
              handle_exec() extracts substring after "cmd=" via strncmp/pointer
              snprintf(shell_cmd, sizeof(shell_cmd), "%s", cmd) buffers the command
              shell_cmd is passed to system()
  transforms: snprintf copy into 1024-byte stack buffer

SANITIZATION (S2 — partial, pipe blocked, semicolon bypass):
  check:      `if (strchr(cmd, '|') != NULL)` → return 403
  bypass:     use ';' as command separator: cmd=true;id>/tmp/pwned
              Note: pass literal ';' in the URL — merecat does not URL-decode
              the query string, so %3B would not be interpreted as semicolon

SINK:        system() in handle_exec() (src/libhttpd.c, injected before httpd_start_request)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/merecat.c — 3 hunks:
    1. global:          added `exec_mode` alongside other global config ints
    2. usage():         added --exec-mode entry in the usage printf block
    3. main():          pre-scan loop compacts --exec-mode out of argv before getopt

  src/libhttpd.c — 2 hunks:
    1. extern decl:     added `extern int exec_mode;`
    2. handle_exec():   new function; I2/S2 implementation (snprintf + pipe check)
    3. httpd_start_request(): exec route guard at the top of the function

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./merecat -n -p 18056 /tmp/www --exec-mode
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18056/exec?cmd=true;id>/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-mode causes /exec to return 404.
  S2 bypass:   pipe is blocked (403), but semicolon is not filtered.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to server stdout/stderr, not the HTTP response body.
    Use write-to-file payloads (true;id>/tmp/pwned) to confirm blind execution.
  - The server runs in foreground mode (-n) to avoid daemonization for PoC use.
  - Use a literal ';' in the URL — merecat does not URL-decode the query string,
    so %3B would not be treated as a semicolon by the shell.
    In a curl command, quote the full URL in single quotes to prevent shell
    interpretation: curl 'http://...?cmd=true;id>/tmp/pwned'
